94139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670808 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670808 1083 #uuid "2d6fd131-4d4b-5c1d-87bc-fd9d9eee9504" 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670809 1068 #edb/ref 17592186670826 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670809 1068 #edb/ref 17592186670833 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670809 1068 #edb/ref 17592186670843 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670809 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670809 1071 "Which of the following first-order linear differential equations are homogeneous?\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670809 1072 #uuid "32e86b1c-ca7c-583b-acda-148bc8829f40" 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670809 1074 "A first-order linear differential equation is homogeneous if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.\n$$\n\nNow, let's consider each equation in turn.\n\n- First, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+4xy=2y.\n$$\n\nWe move the term involving $y$ to the left side so that all $y$-terms are together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}+4xy & =2y \\\\ {y}^{′}+4xy-2y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{′}+(4x-2)y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis matches the homogeneous form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.$ Therefore, this equation is homogeneous.\n\n- Next, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+4xy=3x.\n$$\n\nNotice that this is written in the form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=Q(x)$ where $Q(x)=3x$ is not identically zero. Therefore, this equation is inhomogeneous.\n\n- Finally, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+4xy={x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nNotice that this is written in the form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=Q(x)$ where $Q(x)={x}^{3}$ is not identically zero. Therefore, this equation is inhomogeneous.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}+4xy=2y$ only." 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670810 1075 #edb/ref 17592186670834 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670810 1075 #edb/ref 17592186670844 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670810 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670810 1077 "${y}^{′}+{x}^{3}y=0$" 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670810 1078 #edb/ref 17592186670844 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670810 1079 #uuid "33b0716a-3a08-565d-ab4d-7ef439c1f8bd" 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670811 1080 "true" 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670811 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670811 1083 #uuid "362509b0-7f13-5268-9882-b7458181febd" 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670812 1080 "true" 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670812 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670812 1083 #uuid "3eea5aa8-c67d-5ad3-911c-0f9b71c1f33e" 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670813 1080 "true" 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670813 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670813 1083 #uuid "4a514407-d3f3-575f-b9fa-d8b32140637f" 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670814 1075 #edb/ref 17592186670837 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670814 1075 #edb/ref 17592186670846 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670814 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670814 1077 "${y}^{′}+8{x}^{3}y=-3$" 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670814 1078 #edb/ref 17592186670846 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670814 1079 #uuid "552f7559-74ed-50e1-8505-9c756f346ad2" 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670815 1080 "true" 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670815 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670815 1083 #uuid "5687bd00-e31f-585f-b5c6-ef839794e52e" 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670816 1075 #edb/ref 17592186670818 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670816 1075 #edb/ref 17592186670825 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670816 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670816 1077 "${y}^{′}+{x}^{3}y=-2y$" 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670816 1078 #edb/ref 17592186670818 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670816 1079 #uuid "5c1d467f-a28a-579f-bc4b-7a801f7e6849" 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670817 1068 #edb/ref 17592186670810 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670817 1068 #edb/ref 17592186670816 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670817 1068 #edb/ref 17592186670842 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670817 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670817 1071 "Which of the following first-order linear differential equations are homogeneous?\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670817 1072 #uuid "5f661f26-2894-5b15-9e23-c052d8e0ebda" 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670817 1074 "A first-order linear differential equation is homogeneous if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.\n$$\n\nNow, let's consider each equation in turn.\n\n- First, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+{x}^{3}y=0.\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is already zero, so the equation directly matches the form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.$ Therefore, this equation is homogeneous.\n\n- Next, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+{x}^{3}y=2.\n$$\n\nThe presence of the constant term $2$ means the right-hand side is not zero, and so it cannot be rewritten in homogeneous form. Thus, this equation is *not* homogeneous.\n\n- Finally, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+{x}^{3}y=-2y.\n$$\n\nWe move the term involving $y$ to the left side so that all $y$-terms are together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}+{x}^{3}y & =-2y \\\\ {y}^{′}+{x}^{3}y+2y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{′}+({x}^{3}+2)y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis matches the homogeneous form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.$ Therefore, this equation is homogeneous.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}+{x}^{3}y=0$; ${y}^{′}+{x}^{3}y=-2y$ only." 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670818 1080 "true" 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670818 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670818 1083 #uuid "687d2052-ac77-5d7c-a136-f6f8c22b92d1" 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670819 1075 #edb/ref 17592186670799 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670819 1075 #edb/ref 17592186670815 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670819 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670819 1077 "${y}^{′}+{x}^{3}y=2y$" 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670819 1078 #edb/ref 17592186670815 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670819 1079 #uuid "80dc1c91-c0e8-5a0e-9813-9a770574905c" 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670820 1080 "false" 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670820 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670820 1083 #uuid "885f97b2-8116-577a-b4c8-2fb47506a1a7" 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670821 1080 "true" 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670821 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670821 1083 #uuid "930d61a1-63ff-581c-8958-e9e1eb4da95b" 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670822 1080 "true" 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670822 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670822 1083 #uuid "95337301-0306-5473-a840-a3665a504b75" 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670823 1068 #edb/ref 17592186670814 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670823 1068 #edb/ref 17592186670828 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670823 1068 #edb/ref 17592186670840 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670823 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670823 1071 "Which of the following first-order linear differential equations are homogeneous?\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670823 1072 #uuid "95870580-b5cf-5914-9a93-1e8255bc81ca" 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670823 1074 "A first-order linear differential equation is homogeneous if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.\n$$\n\nNow, let's consider each equation in turn.\n\n- First, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+8{x}^{3}y=4y.\n$$\n\nWe move the term involving $y$ to the left side so that all $y$-terms are together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}+8{x}^{3}y & =4y \\\\ {y}^{′}+8{x}^{3}y-4y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{′}+(8{x}^{3}-4)y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis matches the homogeneous form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.$ Therefore, this equation is homogeneous.\n\n- Next, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+8{x}^{3}y=-5y.\n$$\n\nWe move the term involving $y$ to the left side so that all $y$-terms are together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}+8{x}^{3}y & =-5y \\\\ {y}^{′}+8{x}^{3}y+5y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{′}+(8{x}^{3}+5)y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis matches the homogeneous form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.$ Therefore, this equation is homogeneous.\n\n- Finally, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+8{x}^{3}y=-3.\n$$\n\nThe presence of the constant term $-3$ means the right-hand side is not zero, and so it cannot be rewritten in homogeneous form. Thus, this equation is *not* homogeneous.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}+8{x}^{3}y=4y$; ${y}^{′}+8{x}^{3}y=-5y$ only." 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670824 1080 "false" 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670824 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670824 1083 #uuid "95d22fdd-50a8-58bc-ba28-8ea3cc513275" 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670825 1080 "false" 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670825 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538587 17592186045443 true] [17592186670825 1083 #uuid "9cde3418-92ae-5e09-8723-e8ae6a876